KNOWNBUG
main.cpp
--cpp11
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ string or null: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ array or pointer: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ function or null: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.4\] line \d+ null or array: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.5\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
A conditional expression whose operands are an array (or a function) and
an operand of another type, `b ? "C" : nullptr', was rejected: "types are
incompatible".  [expr.cond]/7 applies the array-to-pointer and
function-to-pointer conversions first; the composite pointer type is then
the pointer type.  g++ and clang++ accept these.
